"===== .claude/FACTORY.md =====
# AI Factory for Claude Code

Generated by ai-factory for **golden-api** (layer: fullstack, profile: golden-profile).

Do not hand-edit anything listed below — re-run \`factory install\` after editing
\`.factory.yaml\` or the profile. Your edits are overwritten otherwise.

## What's here

- \`/CLAUDE.md\` (repo root) — Claude Code auto-loads this. Repo identity, commands, path scoping, profile rules, don't-do list.
- \`.claude/agents/<name>.md\` — 2 subagents. Each runs in its own context with its own tools; editing agents carry a per-agent path-guard hook.
- \`.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md\` — 1 orchestrators. Invoke with \`/<name>\`, or let Claude match your request against the skill's description.
- \`.claude/hooks/\` — the generated guard scripts and their config.
- \`.claude/settings.json\` — **merged, never overwritten**. See below for exactly what the factory puts there.

## Usage

\`\`\`
/feature-factory build invoice reminders for invoices unpaid > 7 days
/quick-fix fix the invoice PDF missing the tenant address
/spike how do we handle Stripe webhook retries?
\`\`\`

Tier 3 runs the full 2-agent chain with three approval checkpoints (story,
brief, final diff). Tier 2 is a single builder. Tier 1 is read-only research. The
skill triages the request first and will suggest a smaller tier if the work doesn't
warrant the full chain.

## Where your settings.json entries came from

Everything the factory adds is derived from \`.factory.yaml\`. Nothing else in the
file is touched, and on re-install only the factory's own entries are refreshed —
your hooks, permission rules and other settings survive.

| Key | Why it's there | Turn it off by |
|---|---|---|
| \`hooks.PreToolUse\` | Runs the path guard on every edit, blocking the \`forbidden:\` list session-wide. | remove \`paths.forbidden\` from \`.factory.yaml\` |
| \`permissions.deny\` | \`Edit(<glob>)\` per forbidden glob. Also covers the file commands Claude Code recognises inside Bash (\`tee\`, \`sed\`, \`> file\`). | remove \`paths.forbidden\` |

## Path scoping — enforced

These agents may only edit their declared paths, enforced by a \`PreToolUse\` hook
in each one's frontmatter: **backend-builder**, **frontend-builder**, **test-verifier**, **migration-author**, **devops-builder**, **doc-writer**. An agent with no list
in \`.factory.yaml\` is unenforced (prompt-only); an empty list means "edit nothing".

The exact globs are in \`CLAUDE.md\` → "Path scoping for agents" and in
\`.claude/hooks/factory-scope.json\`.

**Know the boundary.** The hook fires on \`Write\`/\`Edit\`/\`MultiEdit\`/\`NotebookEdit\`.
A builder also has \`Bash\`, and a shell write never reaches it — the \`permissions.deny\` rules catch the file commands Claude Code recognises, and \`sandbox: true\` catches subprocesses too.
But only the per-agent hook is *per-agent*: a shell write is checked against the
forbidden list, never against an allow-list. Treat per-agent scoping as a guardrail
against the wrong file, not as containment.

## Regenerating

\`\`\`bash
factory install
\`\`\`

Everything above is rewritten from \`.factory.yaml\` and the profile.
\`.factory.yaml\` itself is never touched — it is the one file you hand-edit.

